Sandeep - Of those 3 options you tested a short answer it to use RHIPE, since it provides various advantages over straight streaming, including performance based on my (admittedly limited) testing. A better answer requires evaluating the specific applications you're looking to implement, as well as things like your environment, etc (e.g. physical cluster vs. cloud). The presentation that accompanies the example code on github is here: http://www.slideshare.net/jseidman/distributed-data-analysis-with-r-strangeloop-2011

If you look at the end of the deck you'll note that we provide our recommendations for which tool to use when, so this might help out a little. Also, as we note in the presentation, O'Reilly will very soon be coming out with a book that includes several chapters by Q McCallum on running R with Hadoop. I think this will also be very helpful in understanding the options.

Finally, I'd recommend looking at the rmr package in addition to RHIPE. In my opinion this package is showing significant promise in interfacing R with Hadoop.

Jonathan

