On Oct 21, 2:48 am, Jeremiah Rounds <roundsjerem...@gmail.com> wrote:
> You can basically accomplish everything with streaming if performance
> and file size wasn't an issue. and it is a useful way to go if you
> just want to dabble in R Hadoop interactions to get the idea,  but
> Saptarshi built a number of performance improvements into Rhipe over
> Streaming and also he has made some things more convenient. Once Rhipe
> is setup it is simpler to use then doing everything by hand with
> streaming.  It is sort of an educational and useful exercise to do
> something with streaming once.  Works better with simulations that are
> inherently small data problems but problems such that you can  benefit
> with throwing a lot of cores at them.  For example, some bayesian
> posterior simulations.  The optimizations Rhipe provides are better
> suited toward truly large data problems where you are really going to
> notice them.
>
> On Oct 20, 4:03 pm, Jonathan Seidman <jonathan.seid...@gmail.com>
> wrote:
>
>
>
> > Sandeep - Of those 3 options you tested a short answer it to use RHIPE,
> > since it provides various advantages over straight streaming, including
> > performance based on my (admittedly limited) testing. A better answer
> > requires evaluating the specific applications you're looking to implement,
> > as well as things like your environment, etc (e.g. physical cluster vs.
> > cloud). The presentation that accompanies the example code on github is
> > here:http://www.slideshare.net/jseidman/distributed-data-analysis-with-r-s...
>
> > If you look at the end of the deck you'll note that we provide our
> > recommendations for which tool to use when, so this might help out a little.
> > Also, as we note in the presentation, O'Reilly will very soon be coming out
> > with a book that includes several chapters by Q McCallum on running R with
> > Hadoop. I think this will also be very helpful in understanding the options.
>
> > Finally, I'd recommend looking at the rmr package in addition to RHIPE. In
> > my opinion this package is showing significant promise in interfacing R with
> > Hadoop.
>
> > Jonathan
>
